		"name": "Fulfillor API v1 Copy 3",
		"description": "Public REST API surface for Fulfillor — Login, Product CRUD, Order CRUD.\n\nFlow: run **Auth → Login** first. The test script captures the token into the `api_Key` collection variable, and a collection-level pre-request script injects it as an `api_key` HEADER on every subsequent request — no Postman Authorization-tab config needed.\n\nVariables to set under the collection's Variables tab before use:\n\n- `baseUrl` — e.g. `http://localhost:8080`\n    \n- `username`, `password` — your API user credentials (the user must be in the `FULFILLOR_API` user group)\n    \n- `productId`, `orderId`, `storeId`, `orgId`, `upc` — fixtures for path/body params\n    \n\nAuth model: a single `FULFILLOR_API` user group covers every `/api/v1/\\*` path. Authn = `api_key:` header. Authz uses the existing Moqui `ArtifactAuthz` mechanism. Audit logging falls back to Moqui's built-in `UserAccountHistory` and entity audit-log (no Fulfillor-specific audit entity).",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
		"_exporter_id": "56676757",
		"_collection_link": "https://divyanshu-pichunia.postman.co/workspace/Divyashu-Pichunia-Workspace~5fc969d3-372d-43c2-8bb1-81174aea06b6/collection/28528660-63ed7ffc-a70a-4b79-a87d-16c6eccd72d2?action=share&source=collection_link&creator=56676757"
	},
